---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout>
  <main>

    <header>
      <img src="/profile.jpg" alt="Dmytro Hilei" class="avatar" width="120" height="120" />
      <div class="header-text">
        <h1>Dmytro Hilei</h1>
        <p class="tagline">ML / HPC engineering student at TalTech</p>
        <p class="meta">Tallinn, Estonia</p>
        <p class="meta">
          <a href="mailto:dmytrohilei@gmail.com">dmytrohilei@gmail.com</a>
          <span class="sep">·</span>
          <a href="https://github.com/DmytroHilei">GitHub</a>
          <span class="sep">·</span>
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/dmytro-hilei-1092b3287/">LinkedIn</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section>
      <p class="profile">
        I work on high-performance computing and machine learning. Right now I'm optimizing CUDA
        stereo-matching kernels for Blackwell GPUs in OpenCV
        (<a href="https://github.com/opencv/opencv_contrib/pull/4165">one fix merged upstream</a>)
        and working through Devito, CuPy, MSL, AMD HIP and tinygrad. I'm also interested in computer
        vision, generative language models, and C++/CUDA physical simulations.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Projects</h2>

      <article class="entry">
        <div class="entry-head">
          <h3>Open-source CUDA optimization — OpenCV <code>cudastereo</code> (StereoSGM)</h3>
          <span class="aside">CUDA</span>
        </div>
        <ul class="bullets">
          <li>Mentored by an R&amp;D engineer at SoftServe (mentor's affiliation, not an employer).</li>
          <li>
            Fixed a consistency-check launch-bounds bug that skipped up to a 15-pixel strip on
            non-multiple-of-16 images, merged upstream together with the matching regression-baseline
            update (<a href="https://github.com/opencv/opencv_contrib/pull/4165">opencv_contrib #4165</a>,
            opencv_extra #1392).
          </li>
          <li>
            Implementing <code>TMA</code>/<code>mbarrier</code>-based path-aggregation kernels for
            StereoSGM on Blackwell (<code>sm_100+</code>) GPUs, bit-exact with the legacy kernel; cuts
            the horizontal-aggregation kernel's latency by ~11% (RTX 5060 Laptop) to ~48% (RTX 5090).
          </li>
          <li>
            Reduces end-to-end pipeline latency by up to 5.1% on a rented RTX 5090; open for review,
            awaiting maintainer feedback
            (<a href="https://github.com/opencv/opencv_contrib/pull/4169">opencv_contrib #4169</a>).
          </li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="entry">
        <div class="entry-head">
          <h3>Symbolic music generation with a 462M-parameter Transformer</h3>
          <span class="aside">PyTorch</span>
        </div>
        <ul class="bullets">
          <li>
            Decoder-only autoregressive Transformer (28 layers, d=1152) trained from scratch on
            multi-instrument MIDI (GigaMIDI, Aria-MIDI, Discover), 8.3B notes seen on a single rented
            RTX 5090. Grew out of a 10–20M piano model on MAESTRO and an earlier LSTM baseline.
          </li>
          <li>
            One token per note (pitch, velocity, duration, delta-time on a 20 ms grid), predicted by
            cascaded heads (delta → pitch → duration → velocity) instead of independent ones:
            loss 9.412 vs 9.824 on a 6M model, single seed.
          </li>
          <li>
            RMSNorm + SwiGLU + QK-norm block with RoPE beats the nanoGPT block (val CE 3.137 ± 0.013 vs
            3.886 ± 0.075 at 42M, 3 seeds); trained with Muon and fp8 + <code>torch.compile</code>.
            Conditioning on instrument set and note density costs nothing in loss (1.714 vs 1.716).
            Auxiliary future-prediction heads did not help.
          </li>
          <li>
            Final held-out cross-entropy on clean GigaMIDI: 1.679 per note (pitch 0.367, velocity
            0.497, duration 0.644, delta 0.170), down from 2.242 for the earlier 108M pilot.
          </li>
          <li>
            Now fine-tuning towards Ukrainian pop-rock piano arrangements, using a Demucs +
            basic-pitch pipeline to reduce band recordings to piano.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="links">
          <a href="https://github.com/DmytroHilei/Music_generative_model">GitHub</a>
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="entry">
        <div class="entry-head">
          <h3>Physics-based simulation of wave propagation and heat transfer</h3>
          <span class="aside">C++ / OpenMP / CUDA</span>
        </div>
        <ul class="bullets">
          <li>Numerical PDE solvers for wave propagation and heat diffusion using the finite difference method.</li>
          <li>Parallelized grid computations with OpenMP (AMD Ryzen 9 AI HX 370).</li>
          <li>
            ~20× speedup over the initial CPU-only version through Bentley's-rules-based optimizations
            and memory-usage efficiency, then a further ~11× by porting the kernels to CUDA
            (RTX 5060 Laptop GPU).
          </li>
          <li>Verified correctness against analytical solutions of the PDE.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="links">
          <a href="https://github.com/DmytroHilei/2D_heat_diffusion_and_wave_propagation">GitHub</a>
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="entry">
        <div class="entry-head">
          <h3>Automated GitHub issue-discovery daemon — <code>issuewatch</code></h3>
          <span class="aside">C11</span>
        </div>
        <ul class="bullets">
          <li>
            Single-threaded C11 daemon that polls GitHub issues across watched repos via
            libcurl/HTTP2, prefiltered with a hand-written Aho–Corasick keyword automaton.
          </li>
          <li>
            Batches surviving issues to an LLM (local Ollama or the Anthropic API) for relevance
            judging, then publishes a ranked, self-updating board to a secret Gist with push
            notifications.
          </li>
          <li>Kept cost near zero via ETag caching, incremental watermarking and batched LLM calls.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="links">
          <a href="https://github.com/DmytroHilei/Search_engine_to_find_opensource_issues">GitHub</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Education</h2>

      <article class="entry">
        <div class="entry-head">
          <h3>Tallinn University of Technology (TalTech)</h3>
          <span class="aside">2025 — 2028</span>
        </div>
        <p class="entry-body">BSc in Integrated Engineering. GPA 4.8 / 5.0 (1st &amp; 2nd semesters).</p>
      </article>

      <article class="entry">
        <div class="entry-head">
          <h3>Lviv Physics and Mathematics Lyceum</h3>
          <span class="aside">Graduated 2025</span>
        </div>
        <p class="entry-body">Specialization in mathematics and physics. Average grade 10.8 / 12.</p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Achievements</h2>

      <h4>Olympiads</h4>
      <ul class="bullets">
        <li>
          <strong>Silver Medal</strong> — International Olympiad on Astronomy and Astrophysics (IOAA),
          <a href="https://ioaa2025.in/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/IOAA2025-Final-Result.pdf">2025</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Bronze Medal</strong> — International Olympiad on Astronomy and Astrophysics (IOAA),
          <a href="https://ioaa2024.on.br/assets/pdf/Final_Scores/IOAA%202024%20Final%20scores.pdf">2024</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Silver Medal</strong> — International Olympiad on Astronomy and Astrophysics Junior
          (IOAA Jr),
          <a href="https://www.uoi.ua/en/data/contests/ioaajr/2023/results">2023</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>First-stage diplomas</strong> — All-Ukrainian Olympiads on Astronomy and Astrophysics,
          <a href="https://www.uoi.ua/en/data/contests/uao/2024/results/11">2024</a>
          (<a href="https://space.univ.kiev.ua/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/result2024.pdf">KNU</a>)
          and
          <a href="https://www.uoi.ua/en/data/contests/uao/2025/results/11">2025</a>
          (<a href="https://space.univ.kiev.ua/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/result2025.pdf">KNU</a>)
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h4>Other activities</h4>
      <ul class="bullets">
        <li>
          Member of the Ukrainian scout organization
          <a href="https://plast.org.ua/">Plast</a> for 8 years;
          involved in youth leadership and educational/physical activities.
        </li>
        <li>Jury member for the Ukrainian National Olympiad in Astronomy and Astrophysics.</li>
        <li>Enjoy playing the guitar.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Skills</h2>
      <dl>
        <dt>Programming</dt>
        <dd>Python · C/C++ · LLVM IR · PyTorch · TensorFlow · NumPy · CUDA</dd>

        <dt>ML &amp; vision</dt>
        <dd>Deep learning · transformers · sequence models (RNN, LSTM) · YOLO · FasterRCNN · CNN feature extraction · Vision Transformers (ViT) · OpenCV</dd>

        <dt>Tools</dt>
        <dd>Git · LaTeX · Linux (CLI) · Raspberry Pi 5</dd>

        <dt>Mathematics &amp; physics</dt>
        <dd>Calculus · probability &amp; statistics · astrophysics · finite difference methods for PDEs · numerical simulation · stencil computations</dd>

        <dt>Languages</dt>
        <dd>Ukrainian (native) · Polish (B1) · English (B2+, IELTS 6.5)</dd>
      </dl>
    </section>

  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  main {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2.25rem;
  }

  /* Header */
  header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.35rem;
  }

  .header-text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.1rem;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .avatar {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 120px;
    height: 120px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    object-fit: cover;
    background: var(--avatar-bg);
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0 0 0.15rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--strong);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .tagline {
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .meta {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  .meta a {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .sep {
    color: var(--sep);
    padding: 0 0.15em;
  }

  .profile {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  /* Section headings with a hairline rule, as in the CV */
  h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.35rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--strong);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  h4 {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--strong);
  }

  h4 + .bullets + h4 {
    margin-top: 1.1rem;
  }

  /* Entry: bold title left, date/stack right */
  .entry + .entry {
    margin-top: 1.35rem;
  }

  .entry-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.925rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--strong);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .aside {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    color: var(--faint);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .entry-body {
    margin: 0.15rem 0 0;
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  /* Bullets */
  .bullets {
    margin: 0.3rem 0 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.25rem;
  }

  .bullets li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1rem;
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .bullets li::before {
    content: '·';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0.25rem;
    color: var(--dim);
  }

  .bullets strong {
    color: var(--strong);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .links {
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }

  .links a {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .links a:hover {
    color: var(--strong);
  }

  /* Skills */
  dl {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr;
    column-gap: 1.5rem;
    row-gap: 0.5rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  dt {
    color: var(--faint);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    padding-top: 0.08rem;
  }

  dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85em;
    color: var(--text);
    background: var(--code-bg);
    padding: 0.05em 0.3em;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    header {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 0.9rem;
    }

    .entry-head {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.1rem;
    }

    dl {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      row-gap: 0.15rem;
    }

    dt {
      margin-top: 0.6rem;
    }
  }
</style>
